    41	## Lemma CONE
    42	
    43	Let
    44	
    45	```text
    46	A_t = Q[y]/(H_t),    H_t=12q^2y^2-12q(t+1)y+(t+1)(3t+2),    q=2t+1,
    47	d=2qy-(t+1),         so A_t = Q[d]/(3d^2-(t+1)).
    48	```
    49	
    50	A geometric point of `Spec A_t` means a morphism `Spec K -> Spec A_t`, where
    51	`K` is algebraically closed; equivalently, choose a root of `H_t` in `K`.  At
    52	split indices `t=3s^2-1`, the algebra over `Q` is `Q x Q`, with factors
    53	`d=+s` and `d=-s`, i.e.
    54	
    55	```text
    56	y=(t+1+s)/(2q),      y=(t+1-s)/(2q).
    57	```
    58	
    59	At `t=2`, these are `y=2/5` and `y=1/5`.  Statements over a split index must be
    60	checked factorwise; inverting a nonzero zero divisor in the product algebra is
    61	not allowed.
    62	
    63	On any geometric fibre, write
    64	
    65	```text
    66	I_{t,+}=<T_{t,1},...,T_{t,2t-1}>,      T_{t,0}=c+tau_t,
    67	```
    68	
    69	where `c` is the image of the banked unit and `tau_t` is homogeneous of weight
    70	`4t+1`.  Since the positive rows are homogeneous for weights
    71	
    72	```text
    73	wt(b4)=1, wt(q_{i,0})=i, wt(b3)=t+1,
    74	```
    75	
    76	`Z_+=V(I_{t,+})` is stable under
    77	`lambda.(b4,q_i,b3)=(lambda b4,lambda^i q_i,lambda^(t+1)b3)`.  If `tau_t`
    78	vanishes on `Z_+`, then `T_{t,0}=c` on `Z_+`, and `c != 0` on the fibre, so the
    79	full terminal zero set is empty.  Conversely, if some `x in Z_+` has
    80	`tau_t(x) != 0`, algebraic closedness gives `lambda^(4t+1)=-c/tau_t(x)`, hence
    81	`lambda.x in Z_+` and `T_{t,0}(lambda.x)=0`.  Nullstellensatz gives the
    82	fiberwise equivalence
    83	
    84	```text
    85	<I_{t,+},c+tau_t>=[1]  iff  tau_t in sqrt(I_{t,+}).
    86	```
    87	
    88	If `dim I_{t,+}=0` as a weighted-homogeneous ideal on the fibre, then the cone
    89	`Z_+` is only the origin: any nonzero point would carry a positive-dimensional
    90	`G_m` orbit.  Since `tau_t` has positive weight, `tau_t(0)=0`, so `dim=0`
    91	suffices for (8.1).
    92	
    93	Verdict: **CONFIRMED**, fibrewise for every integer `t>=2`, with the split-index
    94	qualification above.
