    96	## Spine Grading (2.1)
    97	
    98	The charged grading is
    99	
   100	```text
   101	wt(h)=wt(s)=wt(b4)=1,
   102	wt(C_j)=j       (1<=j<=t-1),
   103	wt(q_{j,0})=j   (2<=j<=2t),
   104	wt(T(0))=t,
   105	wt(b_i)=(4-i)t+1, so wt(b1,b2,b3,b4)=(3t+1,2t+1,t+1,1),
   106	wt(y)=wt(g)=wt(g1)=wt(g2)=wt(c)=0.
   107	```
   108	
   109	The symbolic audit checks the coefficient recurrence, not just fixed records.
   110	It verifies
   111	
   112	```text
   113	wt(U_m)=q-m,         wt(C_m)=t-1-m,
   114	wt(B_m)=t-m,         wt(S_m)=2t-m,
   115	wt(V_m)=t+1-m,       wt(Y_m)=2t+1-m,       wt(Z_m)=t+1-m,
   116	wt(P0'_m)=3t-m,      wt(R_m)=4t+1-m.
   117	```
   118	
   119	After the change back from `L=X-b4` to `X`, the factor `b4^(m-k)` gives
   120	`wt(T_{t,k})=4t+1-k` for `k>0`; `T_{t,0}` has the same weight-`4t+1`
   121	nonconstant part plus the scalar `c`.  The audit output is
   122	`SYMBOLIC_WEIGHT_AUDIT = PASS`.
   123	
   124	The finite record audit also passed on all frozen records available for this
   125	lane:
   126	
   127	```text
   128	terminal_laurent_t2,t3,t4,t5: terminal rows and pivot RHS homogeneous;
   129	chart_t3_b4_0, chart_t5_b4_0, chart_t6_b4_0: same after b4=0 specialization.
   130	```
   131	
   132	This covers fixed records for `t=2..6` in the frozen input block.  The `b4=1`
   133	chart records are dehomogenized, so they are not a homogeneity test.
   134	
   135	Verdict: **CONFIRMED**, as an indexed consequence of the Sol recurrence and by
   136	finite record controls through the frozen `t=6` chart.
   137	
   138	## Proposition SUBCHART
   139	
   140	Let `R` be a subset of the residual variables
   141	`{b4,q_{2,0},...,q_{t-1,0},b3}` and let `S` set the complement to zero.  In the
   142	affine solve each eliminated variable `z_w` has the form
   143	
   144	```text
   145	z_w = -rho_w / p_w,
   146	```
   147	
   148	where `p_w` is a weight-zero unit of `A_t` and `rho_w` is homogeneous of weight
   149	`w` in the residual variables, after earlier substitutions by homogeneous
   150	solved values.  On `S`, every monomial involving a killed residual variable
   151	vanishes.  What remains is the span of monomials in `R` whose weights sum to
   152	`w`.  Therefore `z_w|_S=0` if `w` is outside the numerical semigroup generated
   153	by the surviving weights; if there is a unique monomial of weight `w`, the
   154	restriction is a single `A_t` scalar times that monomial.
   155	
   156	This is a grading plus affine-elimination statement.  It does not by itself
   157	assert radical membership in the original multivariable ideal.
   158	
   159	Verdict: **CONFIRMED**, with scope limited to coordinate subcharts after the
   160	weighted affine solve.
   161	
   162	## Theorem B3-AXIS
   163	
   164	Take
   165	
   166	```text
   167	S={b4=0, q_{2,0}=...=q_{t-1,0}=0}.
   168	```
   169	
   170	Then `Sem({b3})=(t+1)Z_{\ge 0}`.  In the high weights `1..2t+1`, the only
   171	surviving high variable is `q_{t+1,0}=lambda b3`; `T(0)`, `b1`, and `b2` have
   172	weights not divisible by `t+1` for `t>=2` and vanish on this subchart.  The
   173	symbolic replay solves the single remaining equation:
   174	
   175	```text
   176	lambda = -(6dt-3d+9t^2+2t-1)/(6t(3t-1)).
   177	```
   178	
   179	The restrictions are
   180	
   181	```text
   182	T_{t,2t-1}|_S = alpha_t b3^2,
   183	alpha_t = t(3t+1)((27t^3-30t^2+t-2)d + (6t^3+13t^2-3t+2))
   184	          /(12(2t+1)^2(3t-1)^2(3t+2)),
   185	
   186	T_{t,t-2}|_S = phi_t b3^3,
   187	phi_t = -t(t-2)(3t+1)(6td-(t+1))/(72(2t+1)^3(3t-1)),
   188	
   189	T_{t,k}|_S=0 for k not in {0,t-2,2t-1}, and T_{t,0}|_S=c
   190	```

