    84	## 1. Lemma CONE: (8.1) is a statement about a weighted cone
    85	
    86	Recall (6.3): with `wt(b4)=1`, `wt(q_(i,0))=i`, `wt(b3)=t+1`, each `T_(t,k)` for
    87	`1<=k<2t` is weighted homogeneous of weight `4t+1-k`, and
    88	
    89	```text
    90	T_(t,0) = c + tau_t,   c = -y g,   tau_t weighted homogeneous of weight 4t+1.
    91	```
    92	
    93	`a1_homog.py` re-verifies this band by band on the charged records and prints
    94	`GRADING_t = PASS` for `t=2,3,4`; it also prints the weight-0 part of band
    95	zero and confirms it equals `c` exactly (for instance `28/625-7y/25` at `t=2`,
    96	which is `-yg` reduced mod `H_2`).
    97	
    98	**Lemma CONE.** Let `K` be an algebraically closed field and `A_t -> K` a ring
    99	map (a geometric point of `Spec A_t`; there are exactly two).  Write
   100	`I_(t,+) = <T_(t,1),...,T_(t,2t-1)>`, `Z_+ = V(I_(t,+)) subset A^t_K` in the
   101	coordinates `(b4,q_(2,0),...,q_(t-1,0),b3)`, and `Z = V(T_(t,0),...,T_(t,2t-1))`.
   102	Then
   103	
   104	```text
   105	Z = empty   <=>   tau_t vanishes identically on Z_+   <=>  tau_t in sqrt(I_(t,+)).
   106	```
   107	
   108	*Proof.* The `G_m`-action `lam.(b4,q_i,b3) = (lam b4, lam^i q_i, lam^(t+1) b3)`
   109	preserves `Z_+`, because every generator is weighted homogeneous of positive
   110	weight.  If `tau_t` vanishes on `Z_+`, then `T_(t,0) = c` on `Z_+` and `c` is a
   111	unit of `A_t`, hence nonzero in `K`; so `Z = empty`.  Conversely let `x in Z_+`
   112	with `tau_t(x) != 0`.  Since `K` is algebraically closed choose `lam` with
   113	`lam^(4t+1) = -c/tau_t(x)`.  Then `lam.x in Z_+` and
   114	
   115	```text
   116	T_(t,0)(lam.x) = c + lam^(4t+1) tau_t(x) = c - c = 0,
   117	```
   118	
   119	so `lam.x in Z`.  The last equivalence is the Nullstellensatz over `K`. `[]`
   120	
   121	**Corollary C1.** `Z_+ = {0}`  =>  `(8.1)`, because `tau_t` has positive weight
   122	so `tau_t(0)=0`.  Since `I_(t,+)` is homogeneous, `Z_+` is a cone through the
   123	origin, hence
   124	
   125	```text
   126	Z_+ = {0}   <=>   dim I_(t,+) = 0.                                   (1.1)
   127	```
   128	
   129	**Corollary C2.** The producer's split is exactly the chart-wise verification
   130	of `Z_+={0}`: `RESIDUAL-ZERO` is `Z_+ cap {b4=0} = {0}` and `TOP-TAIL-UNIT`
   131	implies `Z_+ cap {b4!=0} = empty`.  Lemma CONE shows this is sufficient but not
   132	necessary, and Section 5 exhibits a live failure of necessity at `t=2`.
   133	
   134	Two practical consequences, both used below.
   135	
   136	* Band zero, the row with the largest support and the only inhomogeneous one,
   137	  is removed from the search.  Only its weight-0 part `c`, already a banked
   138	  unit, is used.
   139	* The remaining test is *homogeneous*.  A weighted-degree `std` plus `dim` is
   140	  substantially cheaper than the inhomogeneous unit test on the `b4=1` chart
   141	  that the charged report recorded as `INCONCLUSIVE_TIMEOUT` at `t=5`.
   142	
   143	## 2. The grading on the whole second spine
   144	
   145	The (6.3) grading is the restriction of a grading of the entire post-spine
   146	Laurent chart.  Assign
   147	
   148	```text
   149	wt(h) = wt(s) = wt(b4) = 1,
   150	wt(C_j)     = j        (1<=j<=t-1),
   151	wt(q_(j,0)) = j        (2<=j<=2t),
   152	wt(T(0))    = t,
   153	wt(b_i)     = (4-i)t+1  (i=1,2,3,4),  i.e. 3t+1, 2t+1, t+1, 1,
   154	wt(y) = wt(g) = wt(g1) = wt(g2) = wt(c) = 0.                       (2.1)
   155	```
