    59	### 2.1 The `w`-picture
    60	
    61	Put `w=1/h` and `theta=w d/dw`.  Every polynomial in the charged h-chart is
    62	`h^a f(w)` with `f` a polynomial in `w` whose `w^j` coefficient has weight `j`
    63	in the second grading `wt(h)=1`, `wt(pi)=-t`, `wt(y)=wt(g)=0`, i.e.
    64	`wt(b4)=1`, `wt(q_j,0)=j`, `wt(C_j)=j`, `wt(b3)=t+1`, `wt(b2)=2t+1`,
    65	`wt(b1)=3t+1`, `wt(T(0))=t`.  The charged data are
    66	
    67	```text
    68	U = h^q u(w),        u = 1 + sum_(j=2)^(2t) q_j w^j          (gauge: no w, no w^q)
    69	C = h^(t-1) c(w),    c = 1 + sum_(j=1)^(t-1) C_j w^j,        R = LC, L = h(1-b4 w)
    70	T = h^t tau(w),      tau = g2 + sum_(j=1)^t T_j w^j          (T_t = T(0))
    71	S = h^(2t) sigma(w), sigma = g1 + sum_(j=1)^(2t) S_j w^j
    72	V' = h^(3t) v(w),    v = e + sum_(j=1)^(3t) v_j w^j
    73	utilde = (q-theta)u,
    74	kappa = (1-b4 w)^2 c - y b3 w^(t+1)                        (= Q1/h^(t+1))
    75	psi   = (1-b4 w) sigma - b3 w^(t+1) tau - g b2 w^(2t+1)    (= P1/h^(2t+1))
    76	phi   = (1-b4 w) tau - g b3 w^(t+1)                        (= P2/h^(t+1)).
