   380	## 7. TOP-TAIL-UNIT and RESIDUAL-ZERO: structure proved, certificate not
   381	
   382	**Top tail.**  By (2.4) every top-tail row is quadratic in `b3`,
   383	`T_(t,k)=A_k b3^2+B_k b3+C_k` with `A_k,B_k,C_k` of weights
   384	`2t-1-k, 3t-k, 4t+1-k` in `(b4,q)`, and `A_(2t-1)=alpha_t` is a unit for
   385	`t>=3` (section 3).  Hence `A_t[b4,q][b3]/(T_(t,2t-1))` is free of rank two
   386	and TOP-TAIL-UNIT is equivalent to the statement that the images of
   387	`T_(t,t),...,T_(t,2t-2)` at `b4=1` generate the unit ideal of that rank-two
   388	algebra, i.e. that the `t-1` resultants `Res_(b3)(T_(t,2t-1),T_(t,k))|_(b4=1)`
   389	and the `2x2` minors of the linear parts have no common zero in
   390	`(q_2,0,...,q_(t-1),0)`.  This removes `b3` uniformly; the remaining
   391	statement is a system in `t-2` variables whose coefficients are the
   392	b4-carrying sequences of section 4.  The requested "which auxiliary each row
   393	introduces with a unit leading coefficient" structure does **not** exist in
   394	the charged coordinates: `T_(t,k)` at `b4=1` is not affine in any residual
   395	variable (already at `t=2,y=2/5` the two top rows are two genuine quadratics
   396	in `b3`), so the top tail is killed by resultants, not by a triangular affine
   397	chain.  Exact `TOPT` powers: `b4^7,b4^10` (`t=2`), `b4^21` (`t=3`); modular
   398	`b4^36` (`t=4`), `b4^55` (`t=5`).  The reduction is verified exactly at
   399	`t=3` (`resultant_reduction.py`): the two resultants
   400	`Res_(b3)(T_5,T_4)|_(b4=1)`, `Res_(b3)(T_5,T_3)|_(b4=1)` generate the unit
   401	ideal of `A_3[q_2,0]`, and the `b4=0` resultants generate `(q_2,0^10)`, so
   402	both lemmas are univariate statements there.  The `t=4` instance was started and not completed within the budget.
   403	
   404	**Residual zero.**  Same reduction at `b4=0`: `b3` is integral of degree two
   405	over `A_t[q]` modulo `T_(t,2t-1)|_(b4=0)` (unit `alpha_t`, `t>=3`), so
   406	RESIDUAL-ZERO is equivalent to `V(Res_(b3)(T_(t,2t-1),T_(t,k))|_(b4=0),
   407	k=1..2t-2) = {0}` in weighted `(q_2,0..q_(t-1),0)`-space.  On the b3-axis it is
   408	proved (section 3); in general it is certified for `t=3..6` (exactly at
   409	`t=3,4`, by 5.1 at `t=5,6`) , and by 5.1 at `t=7`, but the axis values carry the pivot
   410	norms (section 4) and no uniform nonvanishing statement was obtained.
   411	
   412	Neither lemma is therefore promoted beyond the finite exact range.
   413	
   414	## 8. Exact residual statement and cheapest test
   415	
   416	Remaining statement (implies (8.1), hence (T) on the ray):
   417	
   418	```text
   419	(V0)  V( T_(t,1), ..., T_(t,2t-1) ) = {0}  in  Abar^t  for every t>=3
   420	      (both roots of H_t; equivalently dim_(A_t) A_t[b3,b4,q]/<T_1..T_(2t-1)> < infinity).
   421	```
   422	
   423	(8.1) itself is the weaker `T^hom_(t,0) in sqrt<T_(t,1),...,T_(t,2t-1)>`,
   424	which is what holds at `t=2,y=1/5` where (V0) fails.  Proved strata of (V0):
   425	the b3-axis for all `t>=3`.  Exact range of (V0): `t=3..6` (and `t=2` on
