@@ -0,0 +1,563 @@
+# K = 16 terminal cone: the \(b_4\)-direction
+
+## Scope, frozen inputs, and verdict status
+
+**Verdict: EXACT RESIDUAL; the requested all-\(t\) promotion is not proved.**
+There are two independent obstructions.
+
+1.  The frozen recurrence gives an exact indexed formula for every pure
+    \(b_4\) coefficient, and exact replay finds every positive-row coefficient
+    to be a unit for \(2\leq t\leq7\).  It does not give a fixed element of
+    \(\mathbf Q(t)[d]\), hence no fixed norm polynomial in \(t\), for any of the
+    requested rows.  The uniform nonvanishing of the indexed numerator remains
+    open.
+2.  Even a uniform unit on the *coordinate axis* would prove only
+    \(b_4\in\sqrt{I_{t,+}+(q_{2,0},\ldots,q_{t-1,0},b_3)}\).  It does not prove
+    \(b_4\in\sqrt{I_{t,+}}\).  The latter is the whole \(b_4\ne0\), or
+    \(b_4=1\), chart and is exactly the missing global statement identified by
+    the charged cone gate.
+
+Thus this lane proves and controls the axis calculation, but it cannot close
+AUDIT delta 17(jjjj) by the proposed implication.  The safe final typing is
+
+```text
+PROVED[INDEXED-B4-AXIS-FORMULA]: all t>=2.
+PROVED[FIXED-B4-AXIS-UNITS]:     t=2,...,7.
+OPEN[B4-AXIS-UNIT-UNIFORM]:     C_t=A_t for every t>=3.
+OPEN[B4-GLOBAL]:                b4 in sqrt(I_{t,+}) for every t>=3.
+```
+
+The last statement is strictly stronger than the preceding axis statement.
+This distinction is already required by Proposition SUBCHART, which explicitly
+does not assert radical membership in the original multivariable ideal
+(`k16-cone-gate-gpt55-20260903.md:138-160`), and by the cone gate's separate
+requirement to control the entire \(b_4\ne0\) chart (ibid.:267-288).
+
+The report skeleton was written before any charged mathematical input was
+read, without a `BODY-END` marker.  I then parsed
+`xmodel/k16-b4-axis-sol56-20260903.run.v2` mechanically with `awk`, pairing its
+`charged_input_<i>_basename` and `_sha256` fields.  The generated manifest
+`box/k16b4-20260903/charged-inputs.sha256` passed `sha256sum -c` on all 23
+frozen files.  No digest was retyped.  Only the listed frozen copies under
+`/tmp/jc2-lane.6VGazO/inputs` were used as mathematical sources; no excluded
+in-progress report, ledger, `jc2-lean`, or `ideation-*` file was read or
+edited.
+
+## 1. Typed setup and coefficient target
+
+Put
+
+\[
+ q=2t+1,\qquad e=3t+1,
+\]
+\[
+ H_t(y)=12q^2y^2-12q(t+1)y+(t+1)(3t+2),\qquad
+ A_t=\mathbf Q[y]/(H_t),
+\]
+and \(d=2qy-(t+1)\).  Then
+
+\[
+ A_t=\mathbf Q[d]/(3d^2-(t+1)).                     \tag{1.1}
+\]
+
+This is a reduced rank-two algebra, not uniformly a field.  It splits as
+\(\mathbf Q\times\mathbf Q\) when \(t=3s^2-1\), with factors \(d=s\) and
+\(d=-s\).  Unit claims at such an index must be checked on both factors.  This
+is the ring declaration and split convention of the charged Sol report
+(`k16-terminal-proof-sol56-20260903.md:45-72`) and cone gate
+(`k16-cone-gate-gpt55-20260903.md:43-61`).
+
+Let
+
+\[
+ R_t=A_t[b_4,q_{2,0},\ldots,q_{t-1,0},b_3],\qquad
+ I=I_{t,+}=(T_{t,1},\ldots,T_{t,2t-1}).
+\]
+
+The weights are
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{wt}(b_4)=1,\quad
+ \operatorname{wt}(q_{j,0})=j,\quad
+ \operatorname{wt}(b_3)=t+1,
+\]
+and \(T_{t,k}\) is homogeneous of weight
+
+\[
+ w_k=4t+1-k\quad(1\leq k<2t).                       \tag{1.2}
+\]
+
+Define the actual axis map, rather than identifying it with an affine chart,
+
+\[
+ \pi:R_t\longrightarrow A_t[b_4],\qquad
+ q_{j,0}\mapsto0,\quad b_3\mapsto0,
+\]
+with kernel \(P=(q_{2,0},\ldots,q_{t-1,0},b_3)\).  Homogeneity gives unique
+coefficients \(c_{t,k}\in A_t\) such that
+
+\[
+ \pi(T_{t,k})=c_{t,k}b_4^{w_k}.                     \tag{1.3}
+\]
+
+The frozen JSON stores \(R=-E_t\), while the question/Sol convention is
+\(T_{t,k}=[X^k]E_t\).  All coefficients recorded here use the latter, so they
+are the negatives of the frozen expressions.  Negating all rows changes
+neither ideals nor norms.
+
+## 2. Mechanical reconstruction of the \(b_4\)-axis rows
+
+### 2.1 Declared rings, maps, and denominators
+
+The evaluator uses pairs for \(a d+b\) in (1.1); multiplication reduces only
+by \(d^2=(t+1)/3\).  It sets \(b_4=1\), \(b_3=q_{2,0}=\cdots=q_{t-1,0}=0\)
+*before* running the charged coefficient arrays.  The value at \(b_4=1\) is
+exactly \(c_{t,k}\) by (1.3), and homogeneity restores the displayed power of
+\(b_4\).
+
+More explicitly, specialize Sol's arrays \(U_m,C_m,B_m,S_m,V_m,Y_m,Z_m,N_m,
+P'_{0,m},R_m\) in equations (2.2)-(2.7).  In weight order
+
+\[
+ z_j=C_j\ (1\leq j<t),\qquad z_j=q_{j,0}\ (t\leq j\leq2t),
+ \qquad z_{2t+1}=b_2,
+\]
+perform the exact affine recursion
+
+\[
+ \widehat z_j=-\widehat\rho_j/p_j,qquad 1\leq j\leq2t+1,              \tag{2.1}
+\]
+where \(p_j\) is respectively the proved closed pivot \(p_C(t,j)\),
+\(p_Q(t,j)\), or \(p_{b_2}\).  Finally
+
+\[
+ c_{t,k}=-\sum_{m\geq k}\binom{m}{k}(-1)^{m-k}\widehat R_m.
+                                                                        \tag{2.2}
+\]
+
+Equations (2.1)-(2.2), together with the finite convolution arrays, are the
+closed symbolic-\(t\) form that is actually proved.  They are not interpolation
+from fixed \(t\).  See `k16-terminal-proof-sol56-20260903.md:78-225` for the
+array proof and `k16-pivot-forms-grok46-20260903.md:82-159` for the pivot
+derivation.
+
+For \(u=a d+b\),
+
+\[
+ N_{A_t/\mathbf Q}(u)=b^2-\frac{t+1}{3}a^2,
+\quad
+ \operatorname{Res}_y(H_t,u)=4q^2\bigl(3b^2-(t+1)a^2\bigr).           \tag{2.3}
+\]
+
+If \(u=(A d+B)/D\), this becomes
+
+\[
+ \operatorname{Res}_y(H_t,u)
+ =\frac{4q^2\bigl(3B^2-(t+1)A^2\bigr)}{D^2}.                         \tag{2.4}
+\]
+
+Thus \(u\) is a unit exactly when the numerator in (2.4) is nonzero.  Formula
+(2.3) is the charged exact resultant calculation
+(`k16-terminal-proof-sol56-20260903.md:265-281`).
+
+Every *division* in (2.1) is safe.  The C-pivot norm is controlled by the
+positive polynomial \(F_C(t,t-n)\), whose displayed expansion has only
+nonnegative terms and positive constant part for \(t\geq2,n\geq1\); the
+Q-pivot norm is controlled by
+
+\[
+ F_Q(t,q-n)=n^2+4nt+6n+4t^2-3\geq12.                 \tag{2.5}
+\]
+
+The last pivot has resultant proportional to
+\(-(t+1)(3t+2)(4t+1)\).  The complete denominator audit and admissible ranges
+are in `k16-terminal-proof-sol56-20260903.md:282-360`.  These facts prove that
+the recurrence is defined; they do **not** prove that an output numerator in
+(2.4) is nonzero.
+
+### 2.2 Closed forms for low and top rows
+
+There is no fixed rational-function closed form in \(\mathbf Q(t)[d]\) for the
+requested \(c_{t,1},c_{t,2},c_{t,2t-2},c_{t,2t-1}\) in the charged
+coordinates.  This is not merely failure to simplify a large expression.
+The first axis pivot already is
+
+\[
+ C_1=\gamma_{t,1}b_4,
+\quad
+ \gamma_{t,1}=
+ \frac{-12dt^2+6dt+72t^3+22t^2-3t+2}
+      {48t^3+20t^2-t+2},                              \tag{2.6}
+\]
+
+and deeper pivots accumulate the growing indexed families
+\(F_C(t,j)\) and \(F_Q(t,j)\).  Because the requested row weight itself grows
+with \(t\), all \(2t+1\) solves can enter.  The charged structural theorem
+therefore identifies the pure-\(b_4\) coefficients as indexed sequences, not
+elements of \(\mathbf Q(t)[d]\); the uniform object is (2.1)-(2.2), with its
+indexed specialization denominator
+(`k16-terminal-proof-fable5-20260903.md:217-272`).
+
+Consequently, “factor the norm as a polynomial in \(t\) and list its integer
+roots” is not a well-typed operation on the present result.  Clearing
+denominators at each fixed \(t\) gives integers \(A_{t,k},B_{t,k},D_{t,k}\)
+and the exact indexed norm numerator
+
+\[
+ \mathcal N_{t,k}=3B_{t,k}^2-(t+1)A_{t,k}^2.          \tag{2.7}
+\]
+
+What would still be needed is a new theorem proving, for example,
+\(\mathcal N_{t,1}\ne0\) for every integer \(t\geq3\), or more generally that
+the coefficient ideal defined below is the unit ideal.  Finite values cannot
+be interpolated into such a theorem under FALLACY-v2.
+
+### 2.3 Norms and unit tests over \(A_t\)
+
+The exact file
+`box/k16b4-20260903/control-axis/axis_exact_t2_t7.json` contains every
+\(c_{t,k}\), in both \((1,y)\) and \((1,d)\) bases, its reduced rational
+denominators, norm, resultant, and unit flag.  Its SHA-256 is
+`2b7b06fd4fbe34d79f64bda69495973486b434c8db62fb4d393ad7f7b801ec15`.
+For compactness, the following table records selected norms as
+`sign (numerator bits / denominator bits)`; every entry is nonzero.  Full
+fractions and SHA-256 identifiers are in
+`box/k16b4-20260903/selected-norm-summary.tsv`.
+
+| \(t\) | \(k=1\) | \(k=2\) | \(k=2t-2\) | \(k=2t-1\) |
+|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| 2 | \(+\ (44/44)\) | \(+\ (31/38)\) | same as \(k=2\) | \(+\ (38/40)\) |
+| 3 | \(+\ (205/204)\) | \(-\ (177/177)\) | \(+\ (141/142)\) | \(-\ (128/131)\) |
+| 4 | \(+\ (347/343)\) | \(-\ (325/324)\) | \(-\ (217/219)\) | \(-\ (207/210)\) |
+| 5 | \(+\ (456/451)\) | \(-\ (418/417)\) | \(-\ (284/286)\) | \(-\ (260/263)\) |
+| 6 | \(+\ (687/681)\) | \(-\ (626/626)\) | \(-\ (396/398)\) | \(-\ (376/380)\) |
+| 7 | \(+\ (1056/1048)\) | \(-\ (1013/1012)\) | \(-\ (611/613)\) | \(-\ (585/589)\) |
+
+In fact every positive-row coefficient, not just those displayed, has nonzero
+norm for each \(t=2,\ldots,7\).  This is an exact fixed-parameter statement and
+is not promoted to all \(t\).
+
+## 3. Exact controls for \(t=2,\ldots,7\)
+
+### 3.1 Comparison with charged Laurent-spine records
+
+The independent pair-arithmetic evaluator checks each measured affine pivot
+against the closed forms before dividing, checks that all bands \(\geq2t\)
+vanish after the \(2t+1\) solves, and emits all \(2t\) terminal values.
+
+| \(t\) | pivot checks | axis result | independent comparison |
+|---:|---:|---|---|
+| 2 | 5/5 | all positive \(c_{t,k}\) units | all 4 frozen JSON rows exact |
+| 3 | 7/7 | all positive \(c_{t,k}\) units | all 6 frozen JSON rows exact |
+| 4 | 9/9 | all positive \(c_{t,k}\) units | all 8 frozen JSON rows exact |
+| 5 | 11/11 | all positive \(c_{t,k}\) units | all 10 frozen JSON rows exact |
+| 6 | 13/13 | all positive \(c_{t,k}\) units | both roots mod 1009, every row |
+| 7 | 15/15 | all positive \(c_{t,k}\) units | both roots mod 1009, every row |
+
+The \(t=2,3,4,5\) comparison is coefficientwise equality with the authenticated
+`terminal_laurent_t*.json`, after the declared global sign.  There are no
+frozen exact \(t=6,7\) row JSON files in this lane, so those lines are exact
+recurrence replays triangulated against the frozen finite-field evaluator on
+both roots, not bytewise row comparisons.  The complete run log is
+`box/k16b4-20260903/control-axis/axis_exact_t2_t7.out`, ending in
+`CONTROL_STATUS=PASS`.
+
+For context, these results agree with the charged cone controls: exact
+dimension zero at \(t=3,4\), the cone-gate exact timeout at \(t=5\), and the
+later fixed-\(t\) characteristic-zero promotions through \(t=7\) in the
+charged Fable report.  Those full-cone results are independent evidence; they
+must not be attributed to the axis calculation.  See
+`k16-cone-gate-gpt55-20260903.md:244-265` and
+`k16-terminal-proof-fable5-20260903.md:318-341`.
+
+### 3.2 The exceptional \(t=2,\ y=1/5\) fibre
+
+Here \(d=-1\).  Exact specialization gives
+
+\[
+\begin{aligned}
+T_{2,1}&=-\frac7{25600}b_4^2
+ (192b_3^2-8960b_3b_4^3+28925b_4^6),\\
+T_{2,2}&= \frac7{640}b_4^4(16b_3-35b_4^3),\\
+T_{2,3}&=-\frac7{640}b_4^3(88b_3-295b_4^3).
+\end{aligned}                                                       \tag{3.1}
+\]
+
+On the \(b_4\)-axis this is
+
+\[
+ (c_{2,1},c_{2,2},c_{2,3})
+ =\left(-\frac{8099}{1024},-\frac{49}{128},\frac{413}{128}\right),   \tag{3.2}
+\]
+so the \(b_4\)-axis is killed on the exceptional fibre.
+
+The exact foreground job
+`box/k16b4-20260903/control-axis/t2_fibre15.sing` was run as
+
+```text
+timeout --kill-after=5s 30s Singular -q \
+  box/k16b4-20260903/control-axis/t2_fibre15.sing
+```
+
+and completed.  Its reduced basis is
+
+\[
+ (b_4^2b_3^2,\ b_4^4b_3,\ 295b_4^6-88b_4^3b_3),
+\]
+with \(\dim R/I_{2,+}=1\) and \(b_4^7\in I_{2,+}\).  All three rows vanish on
+the \(b_3\)-axis.  Hence
+
+\[
+ \sqrt{I_{2,+}}=(b_4),
+\]
+and the cone is exactly the one-dimensional \(b_3\)-axis, while its
+\(b_4\)-axis intersection is just the origin.  This matches the charged
+negative control (`k16-cone-gate-gpt55-20260903.md:215-242`).  Output is in
+`box/k16b4-20260903/control-axis/t2_fibre15.out`.
